{"code":"pt","name":"Portuguese","native":"Português","phase":1,"medium":"en","file_level":"A2","level":{"title":"Elementary: city, travel, routines, health","goals":["Find your way around a Brazilian city","Talk about past trips with pretérito perfeito","Describe routines, health, and future plans"],"units":[{"id":"A2-U1","title":"Getting around","lessons":[{"id":"A2-U1-L1","title":"Around the city (estou no/na)","learn":"Location uses ESTAR: ESTOU EM CASA (I am at home). EM melts: EM+O=NO, EM+A=NA: ESTOU NO BANCO (at the bank), NA PRAÇA (at the square). Esquerda (left), direita (right), em frente (ahead)!","vocab":[{"t":"a rua","r":"ah HOO-uh","en":"street","pos":"noun"},{"t":"a praça","r":"ah PRAH-sah","en":"square","pos":"noun"},{"t":"a estação","r":"ah shtah-SOW(n)","en":"station","pos":"noun"},{"t":"o banco","r":"oo BAH(n)-koo","en":"bank","pos":"noun"},{"t":"o hospital","r":"oo ohsh-pee-TAH-oo","en":"hospital","pos":"noun"},{"t":"a loja","r":"ah LOH-zhah","en":"shop","pos":"noun"},{"t":"a esquerda","r":"ah shkehr-DAH","en":"left","pos":"noun"},{"t":"a direita","r":"ah dee-RAY-tah","en":"right","pos":"noun"}],"grammar":{"title":"ESTAR + em/no/na","explain":"ESTOU = I am, ESTÁ = you/he/she is. EM + O = NO (no banco), EM + A = NA (na praça). ESTOU NO HOTEL = I am at the hotel.","pattern":"estou/está + em/no/na + place","examples":[{"t":"Estou em casa.","r":"shtoh ay(n) KAH-zah.","en":"I am at home."},{"t":"Onde você está?","r":"OH(n)-dee voh-SEH shtah?","en":"Where are you?"},{"t":"A loja é perto.","r":"ah LOH-zhah eh PEHR-too.","en":"The shop is near."}],"mistakes":["Saying SOU em casa — location is always ESTAR.","Saying EM O banco — melt it: NO banco."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Rafael","t":"Desculpe, onde é a estação?","r":"deesh-KOOL-pee, OH(n)-dee eh ah shtah-SOW(n)?","en":"Excuse me, where is the station?"},{"sp":"Ana","t":"É ali, à direita.","r":"eh ah-LEE, ah dee-RAY-tah.","en":"It is over there, on the right."},{"sp":"Rafael","t":"É longe?","r":"eh LOH(n)-zhee?","en":"Is it far?"},{"sp":"Ana","t":"Não, é perto. Cinco minutos.","r":"now(n), eh PEHR-too. SEEN-koo mee-NOO-toosh.","en":"No, it is near. Five minutes."}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: Where is the station?","answer":"Onde é a estação?"},{"type":"fill","q":"Estou ___ casa. (at)","answer":"em"},{"type":"choose","q":"'It is near' is…","options":["É longe","É perto","Estou perto","Sou perto"],"answer":"É perto"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: casa / estou / em","answer":"estou em casa"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Onde é o banco?","answer":"Onde é o banco?"}],"quiz":[{"q":"ESTOU EM CASA means…","options":["I go home","I am at home","my home is big","I like home"],"answer":1,"why":"Estou + em = I am at."},{"q":"À DIREITA is…","options":["left","right","straight","back"],"answer":1,"why":"Direita = right."},{"q":"EM + A becomes…","options":["em a","na","no","numa"],"answer":1,"why":"Em + a melts into NA."},{"q":"ONDE VOCÊ ESTÁ? means…","options":["Who are you?","Where are you?","How are you?","What are you?"],"answer":1,"why":"Onde + está = where are you."},{"q":"CINCO MINUTOS is…","options":["five minutes","ten minutes","five hours","five days"],"answer":0,"why":"Cinco = 5."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"City worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to Portuguese.","items":["street","station","shop"],"key":["a rua","a estação","a loja"]},{"instruction":"Complete with em, no, or na.","items":["Estou ___ casa (at)","Estou ___ banco (at the)","Estou ___ praça (at the)"],"key":["em","no","na"]},{"instruction":"Ask for directions.","items":["Where is the bank?","Is it far?"],"key":["Onde é o banco?","É longe?"]}]}},{"id":"A2-U1-L2","title":"Travel and pretérito (simple past)","learn":"Finished trips use PRETÉRITO PERFEITO: VIAJEI (I travelled), VIAJOU (you/he/she travelled). -AR verbs: -EI (eu), -OU (você/ele/ela). FALEI, COMPROU, CHEGOU!","vocab":[{"t":"a viagem","r":"ah vee-AH-zhay(n)","en":"trip","pos":"noun"},{"t":"o avião","r":"oo ah-VYOW(n)","en":"plane","pos":"noun"},{"t":"o hotel","r":"oo oh-TEH-oo","en":"hotel","pos":"noun"},{"t":"a mala","r":"ah MAH-lah","en":"suitcase","pos":"noun"},{"t":"a passagem","r":"ah pah-SAH-zhay(n)","en":"ticket","pos":"noun"},{"t":"a praia","r":"ah PRAH-yah","en":"beach","pos":"noun"},{"t":"a montanha","r":"ah moh(n)-TAH-nyah","en":"mountain","pos":"noun"},{"t":"a foto","r":"ah FOH-too","en":"photo","pos":"noun"}],"grammar":{"title":"Past -AR: viajei, viajou","explain":"Drop -AR, add -EI (I), -OU (você/ele/ela). VIAJEI = I travelled. COMPROU = you/he/she bought. ONTEM (yesterday) loves this past!","pattern":"stem + ei/ou","examples":[{"t":"Viajei para a Espanha.","r":"vee-ah-ZHAY pah-rah ah sh-PAH-nyah.","en":"I travelled to Spain."},{"t":"Você comprou passagens?","r":"voh-SEH koh(m)-PROH ahsh pah-SAH-zhaysh?","en":"Did you buy tickets?"},{"t":"Ela chegou ontem.","r":"EH-lah sheh-GOH OH(n)-tay(n).","en":"She arrived yesterday."}],"mistakes":["Saying VIAJO for the past — past I = VIAJEI.","Forgetting ONTEM goes with finished past, not present."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Ana","t":"Você viajou este verão?","r":"voh-SEH vee-ah-ZHOH EHS-chee veh-ROW(n)?","en":"Did you travel this summer?"},{"sp":"Rafael","t":"Sim, viajei para o México. Visitei a praia.","r":"seeng, vee-ah-ZHAY pah-rah oo MEH-shee-koo. vee-zee-TAY ah PRAH-yah.","en":"Yes, I travelled to Mexico. I visited the beach."},{"sp":"Ana","t":"Você gostou?","r":"voh-SEH gohsh-TOH?","en":"Did you like it?"},{"sp":"Rafael","t":"Adorei!","r":"ah-doh-RAY!","en":"I loved it!"}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: I travelled to Spain","answer":"Viajei para a Espanha"},{"type":"fill","q":"Você comprou ___? (tickets)","answer":"passagens"},{"type":"choose","q":"'She arrived yesterday' uses…","options":["chega","chegou","cheguei","chegar"],"answer":"chegou"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: visitei / praia / a","answer":"visitei a praia"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Viajei para o México.","answer":"Viajei para o México."}],"quiz":[{"q":"VIAJEI means…","options":["I travel","I travelled","you travelled","he travels"],"answer":1,"why":"-EI = I did (past)."},{"q":"A MALA is…","options":["ticket","suitcase","hotel","beach"],"answer":1,"why":"Mala = suitcase."},{"q":"VOCÊ GOSTOU? means…","options":["Did you like it?","Do you like it?","Will you like it?","You like it!"],"answer":0,"why":"-OU past: did you like."},{"q":"Which is 'you bought'?","options":["comprei","comprou","compra","comprar"],"answer":1,"why":"-OU = you/he/she did."},{"q":"ONTEM means…","options":["tomorrow","today","yesterday","now"],"answer":2,"why":"Ontem = yesterday."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Travel worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to Portuguese.","items":["trip","ticket","beach"],"key":["a viagem","a passagem","a praia"]},{"instruction":"Put VIAJAR in the past.","items":["I travelled","you (você) travelled","she travelled"],"key":["viajei","viajou","viajou"]},{"instruction":"Answer about a trip.","items":["Did you travel? (yes)","Where? (Mexico)"],"key":["Sim, viajei","Viajei para o México"]}]}}]},{"id":"A2-U2","title":"Life and plans","lessons":[{"id":"A2-U2-L1","title":"Daily routines (reflexive verbs)","learn":"Routines bounce back: ME LEVANTO = I get (myself) up. ME = myself, SE = yourself/himself/herself (você!). Mornings run on ME/SE: levantar-se, banhar-se, vestir-se!","vocab":[{"t":"a manhã","r":"ah mah-NYAH(n)","en":"morning","pos":"noun"},{"t":"a tarde","r":"ah TAHR-dee","en":"afternoon","pos":"noun"},{"t":"a noite","r":"ah NOY-chee","en":"night","pos":"noun"},{"t":"o trabalho","r":"oo trah-BAH-lyoo","en":"work / job","pos":"noun"},{"t":"a escola","r":"ah sh-KOH-lah","en":"school","pos":"noun"},{"t":"o banho","r":"oo BAH-nyoo","en":"bath / shower","pos":"noun"},{"t":"o café da manhã","r":"oo kah-FEH dah mah-NYAH(n)","en":"breakfast","pos":"noun"},{"t":"o jantar","r":"oo zhahn-TAHR","en":"dinner","pos":"noun"}],"grammar":{"title":"Reflexive ME/SE: me levanto","explain":"LEVANTAR-SE = to get up. ME LEVANTO (I get up), SE LEVANTA (você/he/she gets up). The little word points back — don't drop it!","pattern":"me/se + verb","examples":[{"t":"Me levanto às sete.","r":"mee leh-VAHN-too ahsh SEH-chee.","en":"I get up at seven."},{"t":"Você se banha de manhã?","r":"voh-SEH see BAH-nyah dee mah-NYAH(n)?","en":"Do you bathe in the morning?"},{"t":"Ela se veste tarde.","r":"EH-lah see VEHSH-chee TAHR-dee.","en":"She gets dressed late."}],"mistakes":["Saying LEVANTO without ME — it means 'I lift', not 'I get up'!","Saying TE (Portugal) in Brazil — Brazil uses SE for você."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Rafael","t":"A que horas você se levanta?","r":"ah kee OH-rahsh voh-SEH see leh-VAHN-tah?","en":"What time do you get up?"},{"sp":"Ana","t":"Me levanto às sete e tomo banho.","r":"mee leh-VAHN-too ahsh SEH-chee ee TOH-moo BAH-nyoo.","en":"I get up at seven and shower."},{"sp":"Rafael","t":"E toma café da manhã?","r":"ee TOH-mah kah-FEH dah mah-NYAH(n)?","en":"And do you eat breakfast?"},{"sp":"Ana","t":"Sim, com minha família.","r":"seeng, koh(n) MEEN-yah fah-MEE-lyah.","en":"Yes, with my family."}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: I get up at seven","answer":"Me levanto às sete"},{"type":"fill","q":"Você se ___? (bathes)","answer":"banha"},{"type":"choose","q":"'She gets dressed late' uses…","options":["me visto","se veste","te vestes","nos vestimos"],"answer":"se veste"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: levanto / me / sete / às","answer":"me levanto às sete"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Me levanto às sete.","answer":"Me levanto às sete."}],"quiz":[{"q":"ME LEVANTO means…","options":["I lift it","I get up","I sit down","I run"],"answer":1,"why":"Levanto + ME = I get myself up."},{"q":"O JANTAR is…","options":["breakfast","lunch","dinner","snack"],"answer":2,"why":"Jantar = dinner."},{"q":"A QUE HORAS…? asks about…","options":["price","time","place","reason"],"answer":1,"why":"A que horas = at what time."},{"q":"VOCÊ SE BANHA means…","options":["I bathe","you bathe","she bathes","we bathe"],"answer":1,"why":"Você + SE = you."},{"q":"Which is reflexive?","options":["falo","me chamo","como","vivo"],"answer":1,"why":"Me chamo = I call myself."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Routines worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to Portuguese.","items":["morning","school","dinner"],"key":["a manhã","a escola","o jantar"]},{"instruction":"Complete with me or se.","items":["___ levanto (I)","Você ___ banha? (you)","Ela ___ veste (she)"],"key":["Me","se","se"]},{"instruction":"Describe your morning.","items":["I get up at …","I shower"],"key":["Me levanto às …","Tomo banho"]}]}},{"id":"A2-U2-L2","title":"Health and future (vou + verb)","learn":"At the doctor: MINHA CABEÇA DÓI = my head hurts. Future with IR: VOU VIAJAR = I am going to travel. VOU, VAI + verb. The plan verb never changes!","vocab":[{"t":"a cabeça","r":"ah kah-BEH-sah","en":"head","pos":"noun"},{"t":"a mão","r":"ah mow(n)","en":"hand","pos":"noun"},{"t":"o olho","r":"oo OH-lyoo","en":"eye","pos":"noun"},{"t":"o médico","r":"oo MEH-dee-koo","en":"doctor","pos":"noun"},{"t":"a farmácia","r":"ah fahr-MAH-syah","en":"pharmacy","pos":"noun"},{"t":"a dor","r":"ah dohr","en":"pain","pos":"noun"},{"t":"a febre","r":"ah FEH-bree","en":"fever","pos":"noun"},{"t":"a saúde","r":"ah sah-OO-dee","en":"health","pos":"noun"}],"grammar":{"title":"Future: vou/vai + verb","explain":"VOU = I go, VAI = you/he/she goes. VOU + verb = I am going to…: VOU COMER = I am going to eat. The second verb never changes!","pattern":"vou/vai + verb","examples":[{"t":"Vou viajar.","r":"voh vee-ah-ZHAHR.","en":"I am going to travel."},{"t":"Você vai estudar?","r":"voh-SEH vey shtoo-DAHR?","en":"Are you going to study?"},{"t":"Vai chover.","r":"vey shoo-VEHR.","en":"It is going to rain."}],"mistakes":["Changing the second verb: VOU VIAJAR, never VOU VIAJO.","Saying EU VAI — I go is VOU."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Rafael","t":"Doutor, minha cabeça dói.","r":"doh-TOHR, MEEN-yah kah-BEH-sah doy.","en":"Doctor, my head hurts."},{"sp":"Ana","t":"Você tem febre?","r":"voh-SEH tay(n) FEH-bree?","en":"Do you have a fever?"},{"sp":"Rafael","t":"Não, mas vou descansar.","r":"now(n), mahsh voh desh-kahn-SAHR.","en":"No, but I am going to rest."},{"sp":"Ana","t":"Bem. Você vai ficar bem.","r":"bay(n). voh-SEH vey fee-KAHR bay(n).","en":"Good. You are going to be fine."}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: I am going to travel","answer":"Vou viajar"},{"type":"fill","q":"Minha ___ dói. (head)","answer":"cabeça"},{"type":"choose","q":"'Are you going to study?' is…","options":["Você vai estudar?","Eu vou estudar?","Ele vai estudar?","Eles vão estudar?"],"answer":"Você vai estudar?"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: descansar / vou","answer":"vou descansar"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Minha cabeça dói.","answer":"Minha cabeça dói."}],"quiz":[{"q":"VOU VIAJAR means…","options":["I travel now","I travelled","I am going to travel","I want travel"],"answer":2,"why":"Vou + verb = going to."},{"q":"MINHA CABEÇA DÓI means…","options":["my head hurts","my hand hurts","my eye hurts","my leg hurts"],"answer":0,"why":"Cabeça = head."},{"q":"A FARMÁCIA is…","options":["hospital","pharmacy","clinic","shop"],"answer":1,"why":"Farmácia = pharmacy."},{"q":"VOCÊ VAI FICAR BEM means…","options":["you were fine","you are going to be fine","you feel bad","you look fine"],"answer":1,"why":"Vai + ficar bem."},{"q":"Which verb NEVER changes in VOU plans?","options":["vou","the first verb","the second verb","both verbs"],"answer":2,"why":"Vou COMER — comer stays whole."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Health worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to Portuguese.","items":["head","doctor","fever"],"key":["a cabeça","o médico","a febre"]},{"instruction":"Write the plan.","items":["I am going to rest","You are going to be fine"],"key":["Vou descansar","Você vai ficar bem"]},{"instruction":"At the doctor.","items":["My head hurts","I have a fever"],"key":["Minha cabeça dói","Tenho febre"]}]}}]},{"id":"A2-U3","title":"Shopping and weather","lessons":[{"id":"A2-U3-L1","title":"Clothes and shopping (este/esse)","learn":"Shop in Portuguese! A CAMISA, OS SAPATOS. Point with ESTE (this, near me) and ESSE (that, near you): ESTA CAMISA (this shirt), ESSE VESTIDO (that dress).","vocab":[{"t":"a camisa","r":"ah kah-MEE-zah","en":"shirt","pos":"noun"},{"t":"a calça","r":"ah KAHL-sah","en":"trousers","pos":"noun"},{"t":"os sapatos","r":"oosh sah-PAH-toosh","en":"shoes","pos":"noun"},{"t":"o vestido","r":"oo vesh-CHEE-doo","en":"dress","pos":"noun"},{"t":"a loja","r":"ah LOH-zhah","en":"shop","pos":"noun"},{"t":"o preço","r":"oo PREH-soo","en":"price","pos":"noun"},{"t":"barato","r":"bah-RAH-too","en":"cheap","pos":"adjective"},{"t":"caro","r":"KAH-roo","en":"expensive","pos":"adjective"}],"grammar":{"title":"ESTE vs ESSE: this vs that","explain":"ESTE/ESTA = this (near me). ESSE/ESSA = that (near you). They match gender: ESTA camisa, ESSE vestido, ESSA loja. (AQUELE = far from both!)","pattern":"este/esta + near thing · esse/essa + your thing","examples":[{"t":"Esta camisa é barata.","r":"EHSH-tah kah-MEE-zah eh bah-RAH-tah.","en":"This shirt is cheap."},{"t":"Esse vestido é caro.","r":"EH-see vesh-CHEE-doo eh KAH-roo.","en":"That dress is expensive."},{"t":"Quanto custa este?","r":"KWAHN-too KOOSH-tah EHSH-chee?","en":"How much is this one?"}],"mistakes":["Saying ESTE camisa — camisa is feminine: ESTA camisa.","Using ESSE for things in your hand — near you is ESTE."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Rafael","t":"Quanto custa esta camisa?","r":"KWAHN-too KOOSH-tah EHSH-tah kah-MEE-zah?","en":"How much is this shirt?"},{"sp":"Ana","t":"Vinte euros. É barata.","r":"VEEN-chee EH-oo-roosh. eh bah-RAH-tah.","en":"Twenty euros. It is cheap."},{"sp":"Rafael","t":"E esse vestido?","r":"ee EH-see vesh-CHEE-doo?","en":"And that dress?"},{"sp":"Ana","t":"Cinquenta euros.","r":"seen-KWEHN-tah EH-oo-roosh.","en":"Fifty euros."}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: This shirt is cheap","answer":"Esta camisa é barata"},{"type":"fill","q":"___ vestido é caro. (that)","answer":"Esse"},{"type":"choose","q":"'That dress is expensive' is…","options":["Este vestido é caro","Esse vestido é caro","Esta vestida é cara","Esse vestida é caro"],"answer":"Esse vestido é caro"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: camisa / barata / é / esta","answer":"esta camisa é barata"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Quanto custa esta camisa?","answer":"Quanto custa esta camisa?"}],"quiz":[{"q":"ESTA CAMISA means…","options":["that shirt","this shirt","those shirts","my shirt"],"answer":1,"why":"Esta = this (feminine)."},{"q":"A CALÇA is…","options":["shoes","trousers","shirt","dress"],"answer":1,"why":"Calça = trousers."},{"q":"QUANTO CUSTA…? asks about…","options":["size","price","colour","place"],"answer":1,"why":"Custa = it costs."},{"q":"ESSE is used for things…","options":["in your hand","near the other person","far from both","invisible"],"answer":1,"why":"Esse = that (near you)."},{"q":"BARATO means…","options":["expensive","cheap","big","new"],"answer":1,"why":"Barato = cheap."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Shopping worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to Portuguese.","items":["shirt","shoes","cheap"],"key":["a camisa","os sapatos","barato"]},{"instruction":"Choose este, esta, esse, or essa.","items":["___ camisa (this)","___ vestido (that)","___ loja (that)"],"key":["esta","esse","essa"]},{"instruction":"Ask prices.","items":["How much is this shirt?","How much is that dress?"],"key":["Quanto custa esta camisa?","Quanto custa esse vestido?"]}]}},{"id":"A2-U3-L2","title":"Weather scenes (fazia, havia)","learn":"Weather stories use IMPERFEITO: FAZIA SOL (it was sunny), HAVIA VENTO (there was wind). Just two phrases paint any past sky!","vocab":[{"t":"o sol","r":"oo soh-oo","en":"sun","pos":"noun"},{"t":"a chuva","r":"ah SHOO-vah","en":"rain","pos":"noun"},{"t":"o frio","r":"oo FREE-oo","en":"cold","pos":"noun"},{"t":"o calor","r":"oo kah-LOHR","en":"heat","pos":"noun"},{"t":"o verão","r":"oo veh-ROW(n)","en":"summer","pos":"noun"},{"t":"o inverno","r":"oo een-VEHR-noo","en":"winter","pos":"noun"},{"t":"a nuvem","r":"ah NOO-vay(n)","en":"cloud","pos":"noun"},{"t":"o vento","r":"oo VEHN-too","en":"wind","pos":"noun"}],"grammar":{"title":"First imperfeito: fazia, havia","explain":"FAZIA SOL/FRIO/CALOR = it was sunny/cold/hot. HAVIA + noun = there was…: HAVIA SOL (there was sun). Weather past = imperfeito, always!","pattern":"fazia + weather · havia + thing","examples":[{"t":"Fazia sol.","r":"fah-ZEE-uh soh-oo.","en":"It was sunny."},{"t":"Havia vento.","r":"ah-VEE-uh VEHN-too.","en":"There was wind."},{"t":"Fazia frio ontem.","r":"fah-ZEE-uh FREE-oo OH(n)-tay(n).","en":"It was cold yesterday."}],"mistakes":["Saying FEZ SOL for scenes — weather stories use FAZIA.","Saying HÁ for past — past needs HAVIA."]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"Ana","t":"Como estava o tempo ontem?","r":"KOH-moo shtah-vah oo TEH(m)-poo OH(n)-tay(n)?","en":"How was the weather yesterday?"},{"sp":"Rafael","t":"Fazia sol. Havia muito sol.","r":"fah-ZEE-uh soh-oo. ah-VEE-uh MOOY-too soh-oo.","en":"It was sunny. There was much sun."},{"sp":"Ana","t":"E hoje?","r":"ee OH-zhee?","en":"And today?"},{"sp":"Rafael","t":"Está chovendo!","r":"shtah shoo-VEHN-doo!","en":"It is raining!"}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: It was sunny","answer":"Fazia sol"},{"type":"fill","q":"Havia ___ (wind)","answer":"vento"},{"type":"choose","q":"'There was sun' is…","options":["Há sol","Havia sol","Fazia sol","É sol"],"answer":"Havia sol"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: sol / fazia","answer":"fazia sol"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Fazia sol.","answer":"Fazia sol."}],"quiz":[{"q":"FAZIA SOL means…","options":["it is sunny","it was sunny","it will rain","it snowed"],"answer":1,"why":"Fazia = was (imperfeito)."},{"q":"A CHUVA is…","options":["sun","rain","wind","cloud"],"answer":1,"why":"Chuva = rain."},{"q":"HAVIA VENTO means…","options":["it is windy","there was wind","wind comes","no wind"],"answer":1,"why":"Havia = there was."},{"q":"Weather in the past uses…","options":["pretérito","imperfeito","future","present"],"answer":1,"why":"Scenes = imperfeito."},{"q":"COMO ESTAVA O TEMPO? asks…","options":["what time was it?","how was the weather?","where was he?","who came?"],"answer":1,"why":"Tempo = weather (also time!)."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Weather worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to Portuguese.","items":["sun","rain","winter"],"key":["o sol","a chuva","o inverno"]},{"instruction":"Paint past skies.","items":["It was sunny","There was wind","It was cold yesterday"],"key":["Fazia sol","Havia vento","Fazia frio ontem"]},{"instruction":"Talk weather.","items":["How was the weather yesterday?","And today?"],"key":["Como estava o tempo ontem?","E hoje?"]}]}}]}],"test":{"title":"A2 final test","items":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: Where is the station?","answer":"Onde é a estação?"},{"type":"fill","q":"Estou ___ banco (at the)","answer":"no"},{"type":"choose","q":"'I get up at seven'","options":["Levanto às sete","Me levanto às sete","Se levanta às sete","Te levantas às sete"],"answer":"Me levanto às sete"},{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: I am going to study","answer":"Vou estudar"},{"type":"translate_t","q":"Minha cabeça dói.","answer":"My head hurts."},{"type":"fill","q":"É ___ (near)","answer":"perto"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: gostou / você / ?","answer":"você gostou?"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: Onde é o banco?","answer":"Onde é o banco?"},{"type":"fill","q":"___ sol. (it was sunny)","answer":"Fazia"},{"type":"choose","q":"'This shirt is cheap'","options":["Este camisa é barata","Esta camisa é barata","Estas camisa são baratas","Esta camisa barata é"],"answer":"Esta camisa é barata"}]}}}